     "response": {
      "pageCount": 2,
      "warnings": [
       "The input XMP declares conformance (pdfuaid/pdfaid) that this output can no longer meet — the structure tree is not carried over yet — so it was dropped rather than copied. Copying it would make the file claim PDF/UA or PDF/A conformance it does not have, which is worse than losing the claim: a validator would then check it against that flavour and fail. Use ensure_tagged + set_metadata on the output to rebuild an honest declaration.",
       "merge_pdfs did not carry over the tagged structure (/StructTreeRoot, /MarkInfo) that the input had (ISO 32000-2 §14.7.2 / §14.8.1): the output is untagged — PDF/UA-1 conformance, reading order, headings and alt text are gone. Assistive technology now sees an unstructured page.",
       "merge_pdfs did not carry over the XMP metadata (/Metadata) that the input had (ISO 32000-2 §14.3.2): only the Info dictionary survives — the pdfuaid/pdfaid identification, dc:title and any PDF/A or PDF/UA claim no longer travel with the file.",
       "These are lost because page copying rebuilds the document from the pages alone. Attachments, /AF, /Lang, /ViewerPreferences and /OutputIntents are carried over; the rest either need the structure tree (B-10c) or depend on page numbers and page references that these operations change. Re-apply the document-level step to the output if you need them (e.g. ensure_tagged / add_bookmarks / set_metadata)."
      ],
      "isError": false
     }
    }
   ],
